The ReSTIR story's shared figures
=================================

What the package's math scenes (script/toy.lam, script/wrs.lam, and the others; lab/src/math/) share, imported as
`paper_restir_common`: the palette every scene colours its symbols by, number formats, a reservoir's record, and a
chance weighed.

$[Import* std]$[Import* render_lab_runtime]$[Import* render_lab_math]

The cheap choice's probability p, the target p-hat, a candidate's weight w, the true total, and an estimate.
$[# pColor [% {rgb "#8fb8ff"}]]

$[# targetColor [% {rgb "#ffd166"}]]

$[# weightColor [% {rgb "#ff6fb5"}]]

$[# totalColor [% {rgb "#6be3b0"}]]

$[# estimateColor [% {rgb "#ffa14a"}]]

Fn([Float], String). A number as LaTeX: a fraction with the smallest denominator up to 16 that makes it whole
(4/3, 20/3), else two decimals.
$[# {rational x}
    [# {_try d} {!if {> d 16}
        {numberLatex x 2}
        {!if {< {abs {- {* x {float d}} {float {round {* x {float d}}}}}} 0.000001}
            {fractionLatex {round {* x {float d}}} d}
            {_try {+ d 1}}}}]
    {_try 1}]

Fn([List(Mob), Float, Vec2, Float], List(Mob)). A figure moved toward `to` and scaled toward `scale` as `t` runs.
$[# toward {: {^ {mobs scale to t}
    [# k {smooth {clamp t 0.0 1.0}}]
    {moveTo
        {scaled mobs {lerp 1.0 scale k}}
        {lerp2 {centerOf mobs} to k}}} {Fn {' {List Mob} Float Vec2 Float} {List Mob}}}]

Fn([Int], String). The kept candidate's name as LaTeX (x_i), or nothing while none is kept.
$[# {keptName k} {!if {< k 0} "" f"{x_{${str {+ k 1}}}}"}]

Fn([Float, Float], Float). `a` over `b`, or 0 when `b` is 0 (a candidate behind P's surface weighs nothing).
$[# {over a b} {!if {> b 0.0} {/ a b} 0.0}]

Fn([Float], String). A weight as LaTeX, to three significant figures (two decimals at least, six at most).
$[# {short x}
    [# digits {!if {<= x 0.0} 2 {clamp {- 2 {floor {/ {ln x} {ln 10.0}}}} 1 6}}]
    {numberLatex x {!if {>= x 10.0} 1 digits}}]

Fn([Vec2, String, String, String, String, Float], List(Mob)). A record at `at` showing `kept`, `sum`, and `count`
(LaTeX; empty strings leave a field blank), its fields named under `id` and captioned, `alpha` its frame's.
$[# record {:
    {^ {id at kept sum count}
        [# box3 {box {sub2 at {v2 2.7 0.55}} {add2 at {v2 2.7 0.55}}}]
        [# xs {' -1.8 0.0 1.8}]
        [# {_field k key value}
            [# c {add2 at {v2 {nth xs k} 0.0}}]
            {append
                {moveTo
                    {caption {++ id {++ "Cap" {str k}}} key 0.3 textDimColor}
                    {add2 c {v2 0.0 0.85}}}
                {!if {= value ""}
                    {'}
                    {moveTo {tex {++ id {++ "F" {str k}}} value 0.44 textColor} c}}}]
        {flatten {'
            {outlined {++ id "Box"} box3 textColor 2.5}
            {line
                {++ id "Rule"}
                {add2 at {v2 -0.9 -0.55}}
                {add2 at {v2 -0.9 0.55}}
                textDimColor
                1.5}
            {line {++ id "Rule"} {add2 at {v2 0.9 -0.55}} {add2 at {v2 0.9 0.55}} textDimColor 1.5}
            {_field 0 {textKey "wrsmath-kept"} kept}
            {_field 1 {textKey "wrsmath-sum"} sum}
            {_field 2 {textKey "wrsmath-count"} count}}}}
    {Fn {' String Vec2 String String String} {List Mob}}}]

Fn([String, Float, Float, Float, Bool, Float, Vec2], List(Mob)). A chance weighed at progress `t`, about `at`: the
fraction `left` (LaTeX) with its numbers, `w` over `total`, the chance as a lit part of a bar from 0 to 1, and the
number `u` the update drew dropping onto the bar (inside the lit part, `taken`: the new one replaces the kept one), and
once it lands (from 76 %), the comparison it made, `u` against the chance, under the bar.
$[# chanceView {:
    {^ {left w total u taken t at}
        [# c {over w total}]
        [# formula {moveTo
            {texParts "chanceF" f"{\lit{1}{$left} = \frac{\lit{2}{${short w}}}{\lit{3}{${short total}}} = \lit{4}{${numberLatex c 2}}}" 0.4 textColor
                {' "left" "wv" "sv" "c"}
                {' textColor weightColor textColor estimateColor}}
            at}]
        [# y {- {.y at} 1.8}]
        [# bar {chanceBar "chance"
            {box {v2 {- {.x at} 2.0} {- y 0.14}} {v2 {+ {.x at} 2.0} {+ y 0.14}}}
            c
            u
            taken
            t
            estimateColor}]
        [# verdict {moveTo
            {tex "chanceVerdict"
                {!if taken
                    f"{u = ${numberLatex u 2} < ${numberLatex c 2}}"
                    f"{u = ${numberLatex u 2} \ge ${numberLatex c 2}}"}
                0.36
                {!if taken accentColor textColor}}
            {v2 {.x at} {- y 0.85}}}]
        {flatten {'
            {fadeIn {phase t 0.0 0.2} formula}
            bar
            {!if {>= t 0.76} {fadeIn {phase t 0.76 0.82} verdict} {'}}}}}
    {Fn {' String Float Float Float Bool Float Vec2} {List Mob}}}]

Fn([Float, List(Mob), List(String), Color], List(Mob)). A figure with its parts named in `ids` pointed at while `t`
runs (`indicate` on those parts alone; the figure as it is before and after).
$[# {pointParts t mobs ids color} {!if {!and {> t 0.0} {< t 1.0}}
    {append
        {filter mobs {^ {m} {not {contains ids {idOf m}}}}}
        {indicate t {filter mobs {^ {m} {contains ids {idOf m}}}} color}}
    mobs}]

Fn([Float, List(Mob), List(String), Color], List(Mob)). A figure with its parts named in `ids` struck out (`t`).
$[# {crossParts t mobs ids color} {append
    {filter mobs {^ {m} {not {contains ids {idOf m}}}}}
    {crossOut t {filter mobs {^ {m} {contains ids {idOf m}}}} color}}]

Steps as clips

A math scene of this package goes through steps, one per sentence of its beat (or a part of one). Each step `k` is a
progress of the scene's own, `<scene>.<k>`, from 0 to 1, and a clip moves it (lab/src/clip.rs): the story plays a
step's clip over its sentence's words (`playOver…`), and a beat that starts the scene sets every step where the
beat begins (`play…`). The scene reads where it is from them (`stepOf`).

Fn([String, Int], String). The progress of step `k` of the scene `name`.
$[# {_stepKey name k} {++ name {++ "." {str k}}}]

Fn([String, Int], Float). Where the scene `name` of `count` steps is: the furthest step a clip has moved, its
number before it plus its progress (5.4: step 6 four tenths done). A scene no clip has set yet (a demonstration
opened on it) is at its end, `count`, as the finished picture.
$[# stepOf {: {^ {name count}
    [# ks {range 1 {+ count 1}}]
    {!if {any ks {^ {k} {hasProgress {_stepKey name k}}}}
        {fold ks 0.0 {^ {m k}
            [# p {progress {_stepKey name k}}]
            {!if {> p 0.0} {max m {+ {float {- k 1}} p}} m}}}
        {float count}}} {Fn {' String Int} Float}}]

Fn([String, Int, Float, Float], Clip). Step `k` of the scene `name` from `a` to `b` of it (0 to 1, the whole
step), over a second, eased as a story's range is (`smooth`).
$[# stepClip {: {^ {name k a b} {clip {'
    {progressKeys
        {_stepKey name k}
        {'
            {keyframe 0.0 a "linear"}
            {keyframe 1.0 b "smooth"}}}}}} {Fn {' String Int Float Float} Clip}}]

Fn([String, Int, Int], Clip). The scene `name` of `count` steps set at once to the end of step `n`: the steps up
to it done, the others not begun.
$[# stepsAt {: {^ {name count n} {clip {map
    {range 1 {+ count 1}}
    {^ {k} {progressKeys
        {_stepKey name k}
        {' {keyframe 0.0 {!if {<= k n} 1.0 0.0} "linear"}}}}}}} {Fn {' String Int Int} Clip}}]

Fn([String, Int], Clip). Every step of the scene `name` of `count` steps in order from none, a second each: its
demonstration's Play. Each step's progress is 0 from the start until its second, then rises to 1.
$[# stepsInOrder {: {^ {name count} {clip {map
    {range 1 {+ count 1}}
    {^ {k}
        [# begins {float {- k 1}}]
        {progressKeys
            {_stepKey name k}
            {'
                {keyframe 0.0 0.0 "linear"}
                {keyframe begins 0.0 "linear"}
                {keyframe {+ begins defaultSeconds} 1.0 "smooth"}}}}}}} {Fn {' String Int} Clip}}]

Fn([Float], Float). Where smootherstep reaches `y` (0 to 1), by halving.
$[# {_unsmooth y} {.first {fold
    {range 0 40}
    {pair 0.0 1.0}
    {^ {r e}
        [# mid {/ {+ {.first r} {.second r}} 2.0}]
        {!if {< {smooth mid} y} {pair mid {.second r}} {pair {.first r} mid}}}}}]

Fn([String, Float, Float], Clip). The scene `name` from `a` to `b` across several steps over a second, as one
smooth range: each step's progress moves while the whole passes through it, through sixteen keyframes on the
curve (a close fit to the range's easing, not an exact one).
$[# stepsRun {: {^ {name a b}
    [# {at x} {+ a {* {- b a} {smooth x}}}]
    [# first {+ {floor a} 1}]
    [# last {ceil b}]
    {clip {map
        {range first {+ last 1}}
        {^ {k}
            [# lo {max a {float {- k 1}}}]
            [# hi {min b {float k}}]
            [# x0 {_unsmooth {/ {- lo a} {- b a}}}]
            [# x1 {_unsmooth {/ {- hi a} {- b a}}}]
            {progressKeys
                {_stepKey name k}
                {map
                    {range 0 17}
                    {^ {i}
                        [# x {+ x0 {* {- x1 x0} {/ {float i} 16.0}}}]
                        {keyframe x
                            {clamp {- {at x} {float {- k 1}}} 0.0 1.0}
                            "linear"}}}}}}}} {Fn {' String Float Float} Clip}}]
